;; Top-level tools coordinator (rf2-nuuk3).
;;
;; The published artefacts, grouped by the channel they actually ship
;; on — the three are gated differently and the flat list this note
;; used to carry hid that (rf2-gugc3):
;;
;;   Clojars, per-tool tag, in the lockstep inventory
;;   (.github/scripts/verify-version-lockstep.sh TOOLS — these five and
;;   only these five):
;;   - xray/         (day8/re-frame2-xray)
;;   - story/        (day8/re-frame2-story)
;;   - story-mcp/    (day8/re-frame2-story-mcp)
;;   - machines-viz/ (day8/re-frame2-machines-viz)
;;   - mcp-base/     (day8/re-frame2-mcp-base)
;;
;;   Each of those five has a release workflow. story, story-mcp and
;;   mcp-base share ONE glob (`story-v*`, release-story.yml) because
;;   they are a shipping set with a dependency order between them:
;;   mcp-base and story deploy first, story-mcp last (rf2-4u3t1,
;;   rf2-2ii52). xray and machines-viz have a glob each.
;;
;;   npm, not Clojars, no :clein/build, deliberately outside the
;;   lockstep inventory:
;;   - re-frame2-pair-mcp/  (@day8/re-frame2-pair-mcp)
;;
;;   git coordinate on a template-v* tag, not Clojars, guarded by its
;;   own in-template version_lockstep_test.clj rather than by the
;;   repo-level script (rf2-40vmd / rf2-dolpf §2.5):
;;   - template/     (day8/re-frame2-template)
;;
;; see tools/xray/deps.edn, tools/machines-viz/deps.edn,
;; tools/mcp-base/deps.edn, tools/re-frame2-pair-mcp/deps.edn,
;; tools/story/deps.edn, tools/story-mcp/deps.edn, and
;; tools/template/deps.edn. The operational runbook for all of it is
;; docs/release-process.md §The tools tier.
;;
;; Other tool directories (machines-viz-mcp/, mcp-conformance/) are
;; spec-only or Node-only today — no `deps.edn` / CLJ surface to
;; coordinate. They will be added here when their `src/` trees land.
;; The Node-side `tools/mcp-conformance/wire-vocab/deps.edn` is a
;; self-contained JVM conformance test; it is run from its own
;; directory and is not coordinated here.
;;
;; ## machines-viz is shipped (rf2-o9arp), NOT collapsed (rf2-z0cw6s)
;;
;; A prior note here said `tools/machines-viz/` had been COLLAPSED
;; (rf2-yamkm — Mermaid relocated, chart role absorbed by Xray). That is
;; STALE. rf2-o9arp REVIVED machines-viz as its own published artefact:
;; `tools/machines-viz/deps.edn` declares real `:paths ["src"]`, a
;; runtime transit-cljs dep, a `:test` alias, and a `:clein/build` for
;; `day8/re-frame2-machines-viz` with the SAME lockstep posture as Xray.
;; Xray now CONSUMES machines-viz (its Machine Inspector re-exports the
;; chart via thin shims), rather than owning the chart. The Mermaid
;; emitter lives in THIS jar again (rf2-sqhqu), not implementation/machines.
;;
;; ## What this file is — and what it is NOT (rf2-6r9j.139 / .140)
;;
;; A CLASSPATH coordinator, and nothing more: `:paths []` plus one
;; `:local/root` per tool artefact, so a REPL started from `tools/` sees the
;; whole tool tier on one classpath. It is not a published artefact and it
;; declares NO test alias.
;;
;; It used to carry an aggregate `:test` alias advertised as covering "every
;; JVM-runnable tool". It did not. Its `:extra-paths` and runner `-d` list
;; named only xray, mcp-base, story, story-mcp and template, while
;; machines-viz (whose `engine_grammar_parity_test.cljc` and
;; `mermaid_public_smoke_test.cljc` have no other JVM lane),
;; testbed-support and mcp-conformance/wire-vocab were silently absent —
;; and no CI job ever ran the alias, so nothing could make the drift red. A
;; developer running the advertised single-command sanity check got a green
;; that skipped live JVM-only contracts.
;;
;; The roster that IS maintained, and IS held against the required CI jobs by
;; scripts/check_jvm_lane_rosters.py, is `scripts/test-jvm-tools.sh`. That is
;; the tool-tier JVM command. A second hand-written inventory beside it bought
;; a convenience whose only distinguishing property was being wrong, so it is
;; gone rather than duplicated more carefully (rf2-6r9j.139).
;;
;; A sibling `tools/shadow-cljs.edn` retired with it for the same reason
;; (rf2-6r9j.140): it mirrored two of Pair MCP's builds, never grew the
;; `descriptor-gen` build Pair added afterwards nor the CLJS lanes mcp-base
;; and machines-viz added, and had no workflow, npm script or gate invoking
;; it. Every tool with a CLJS surface owns an adjacent `shadow-cljs.edn`, and
;; those are what CI and the npm scripts already run.
;;
;; ## Why template is NOT in the base :deps map
;;
;; `tools/template/` ships deps-new template resources — the `resources/`
;; tree contains placeholder-bearing `.cljs` files (e.g.
;; `(ns {{top/ns}}.{{main/ns}}...)` in
;; resources/day8/re_frame2_template/_shared/src/events_test.cljs) that
;; are NOT valid ClojureScript. Anything that READS that tree as SOURCE
;; rather than as opaque resources fails at the read loop, so the template
;; artefact is kept off this classpath, and `tools/template/resources/` is
;; excluded explicitly from the clj-kondo and Splint invocations in
;; .github/workflows/lint.yml. The template's own tests run from
;; `tools/template` (`clojure -M:test`), on the JVM, where the `.cljs`
;; templates are plain resources.
;;
;; ## Bundle-isolation
;;
;; This file does NOT change the tool→implementation dependency arrow
;; (see tools/README.md §The bundle-isolation contract). It only widens
;; the *coordinator's* classpath; nothing under implementation/ may
;; :require anything under tools/.
{:paths []
 :deps  {day8/re-frame2-xray         {:local/root "xray"}
         day8/re-frame2-machines-viz {:local/root "machines-viz"}
         day8/re-frame2-mcp-base     {:local/root "mcp-base"}
         day8/re-frame2-pair-mcp     {:local/root "re-frame2-pair-mcp"}
         day8/re-frame2-story        {:local/root "story"}
         day8/re-frame2-story-mcp    {:local/root "story-mcp"}}}
